TITLE:: NdefRackCommentView
summary:: a box of text on the rack
categories:: Libraries>NdefRack
related:: Classes/NdefRackGUI, Classes/NdefRack

DESCRIPTION::
One comment of link::Classes/NdefRack#*comments::, drawn by the window in the
rack's coordinates at the window's zoom. It is the window's, like a module's
place: nothing about it reaches an Ndef, and a patch file keeps it. You make
comments with the window's strong::+ comment::, its rack menu's strong::comment
here::, or code::NdefRack.addComment::; the window makes and frees the views.

table::
## click || select it; backspace then deletes it
## drag || move it, on the 10 pixel grid
## drag the bottom right corner || resize it
## double click || a field to write in: cmd-return or a click elsewhere keeps what is written, escape leaves it as it was
## right click || write in it, delete it
::

Text wraps at the box's width. A flow chart cable goes round it
(link::Classes/NdefRackRouter::).

code::
NdefRack.addComment("the loop: seed, fold, split, tilt, back", Point(40, 20), Point(300, 50));
NdefRack.gui;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Made by the window.
ARGUMENT:: gui
The link::Classes/NdefRackGUI::.
ARGUMENT:: id
The comment's id in link::Classes/NdefRack#*comments::.

METHOD:: minSize
The smallest it can be resized to. 60 @ 30.

METHOD:: grip
How big the corner that resizes it is, in pixels. 12.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: text
What it says, from NdefRack.

METHOD:: bounds
Where it is, a link::Classes/Rect:: in the rack's coordinates.

METHOD:: origin
Its top left, in the rack's coordinates.

METHOD:: size
Its width and height.

METHOD:: edit
Open the field to write in it.

METHOD:: isEditing
Whether the field is open.

METHOD:: editor
The field while it is open, a link::Classes/TextView::, else nil.

METHOD:: follow
Take where it is and what it says from NdefRack again: the window does this when
a comment changes in code.

METHOD:: gui
The window.

METHOD:: id
Its id.

METHOD:: view
Its link::Classes/UserView::.

METHOD:: refresh
Draw it again.

METHOD:: front
Raise it above its siblings.

METHOD:: remove
Remove its view.
